01:54:31.210 --> 01:54:33.930
expanded services to serve additional residents.

01:54:34.250 --> 01:54:37.290
And so it's not just a net new impact.

01:54:37.770 --> 01:54:41.290
The other thing is that that assessment growth Revenue also

01:54:41.790 --> 01:54:45.490
builds the capacity to renew the growth, the infrastructure that is

01:54:45.990 --> 01:54:49.530
built with development charges up front down the road

01:54:49.610 --> 01:54:53.130
as those that infrastructure ages, that contributes

01:54:53.630 --> 01:54:57.650
to the renewal dollars. So that is why there is a separate revenue stream for

01:54:58.150 --> 01:55:01.850
building that growth enabling infrastructure. So to suggest that assessment

01:55:02.350 --> 01:55:05.810
growth revenue should be used for growth enabling infrastructure,

01:55:06.050 --> 01:55:08.210
I think is not quite correct.

